From 978ab77844aad698a5333f9223c02350de43b8df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:54:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] RISC OS: present only what changed

VCMI uploads the whole screen to a texture every frame and has SDL's
renderer scale and present it. On RISC OS that's SDL's software renderer,
its slowest path (the Julius port started at 13 fps that way). Instead:

- riscos/riscos_present: a shadow copy of the last frame, 64x16 pixel
  cells compared a word (or 16 pixels with NEON) at a time, changed cells
  merged into rectangles, nearest scaling by tables, XBGR conversion,
  straight into the window surface (SDL_UpdateWindowSurfaceRects). The
  software pointer is blended in. Statistics in the log every 10 s.
- The SDL renderer stays (software): its logical size maps the mouse.
- The frame limiter waits in SDL_Delay (Wimp_PollIdle: the desktop gets
  the time), again while 5 ms or more remain.
- Defaults: software renderer and pointer, no vsync (it switched the
  limiter off), 50 frames a second, no xBRZ, nearest scaling, no intro.
